WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:09.264 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to Sweden's regions, part 1 of 1. First, I clear the chosen names for
a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:21.269 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
We work through 21 of the Sweden regions the map names, once each: where it
sits, one fact worth keeping, and a hook to remember it by.

3
00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:23.891 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Norrbotten into view.

4
00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:42.840 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Norrbotten fills the far north of Sweden, running from the mountains in the
west down to the head of the Gulf of Bothnia in the east, with Luleå on the
coast and only Västerbotten below it in the south.

5
00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:54.976 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The iron mine at Kiruna is the largest underground mine in the world, and
because the mining is hollowing out the ground beneath the town, Kiruna is
being moved building by building to the east.

6
00:00:55.639 --> 00:01:04.683 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the northern bottom, the head of the gulf of Bothnia, where the whole
town is being shifted sideways so the mine can keep digging.

7
00:01:05.363 --> 00:01:08.126 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Västerbotten into view.

8
00:01:12.932 --> 00:01:22.824 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Västerbotten is the coastal county below Norrbotten on the Gulf of Bothnia,
with Umeå on the shore and the mountains rising inland to the west, towards
Jämtland and the Norwegian border.

9
00:01:23.486 --> 00:01:33.587 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its Västerbottensost cheese is made to a recipe the dairy keeps secret, and it
is what Swedes eat with cured roe at the August crayfish parties.

10
00:01:34.239 --> 00:01:48.786 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the western side of that bottom, the county of the secret cheese and
the town where every street has birch trees planted after the fire of 1888.

11
00:01:49.478 --> 00:01:51.568 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Jämtland into view.

12
00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:10.574 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Jämtland is the wide inland county in the west of the country, landlocked and
long, with a long border on Norway to the north-west and Östersund on the
great lake Storsjön in the middle.

13
00:02:11.236 --> 00:02:24.541 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It was Norwegian until 1645, and at Midsummer every year the county still
proclaims a symbolic republic of Jämtland, with a president and a border post
of its own.

14
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:37.181 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the little republic in the western mountains, with Åre’s ski slopes
above Storsjön and a monster in the lake that was protected until 2005.

15
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.643 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Västernorrland into view.

16
00:02:45.151 --> 00:02:57.690 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Västernorrland sits on the Gulf of Bothnia between Västerbotten in the north
and Gävleborg in the south, with Sundsvall on the coast and Jämtland inland to
the west.

17
00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:09.857 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its High Coast has risen about 286 metres since the ice melted and still lifts
about eight millimetres a year, the greatest such uplift measured anywhere.

18
00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:21.943 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the western Norrland coast that is still rising, and Sundsvall, the
stone city rebuilt from scratch after the fire of 1888.

19
00:03:22.624 --> 00:03:25.132 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Gävleborg into view.

20
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:38.934 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Gävleborg faces the Gulf of Bothnia in the middle of Sweden’s long east coast,
with Gävle on the shore, Västernorrland above it and Uppsala below it.

21
00:03:39.593 --> 00:03:49.659 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Seven of its Hälsingland farmhouses are a UNESCO world heritage site, and
their rooms are painted from floor to ceiling by travelling artists.

22
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:59.236 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the coast of the painted farmhouses, and the giant straw goat in
Gävle that arsonists have burned down more often than not.

23
00:03:59.944 --> 00:04:02.371 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Dalarna into view.

24
00:04:09.096 --> 00:04:20.567 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Dalarna lies inland in the middle-west of Sweden, a long county of lake and
forest around the valley of the Dalälven, with Borlänge in its southern half
and no sea at all.

25
00:04:21.228 --> 00:04:31.120 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The painted wooden Dala horse from Nusnäs is the unofficial symbol of Sweden,
carved since the 1600s to pass the long winter evenings.

26
00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:41.152 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the dales of the Dalälven, the little red and white horse from
Nusnäs, and the mine waste that still paints Swedish houses red.

27
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.837 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Uppsala into view.

28
00:04:49.564 --> 00:05:01.592 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Uppsala lies just north of Stockholm on the Baltic, with its largest city,
Uppsala, on the Fyris river between Lake Mälaren and the sea, and Stockholm
county to the south.

29
00:05:02.256 --> 00:05:13.773 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its university, founded in 1477, is the oldest in Scandinavia, and Linnaeus
taught there, his garden still planted to his own plan.

30
00:05:14.428 --> 00:05:23.344 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the upper halls of the old kings, the pagan burial mounds of Gamla
Uppsala and the garden of the great doctor of plants.

31
00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.039 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Värmland into view.

32
00:05:31.318 --> 00:05:43.346 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Värmland is the inland county in the west of the country, north of Lake
Vänern, with Karlstad where the Klarälven runs into the lake, and Norway on
its western edge.

33
00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:53.854 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Selma Lagerlöf, the first woman to win the Nobel Prize in Literature, was born
here and set her novels among these lakes and forests.

34
00:05:54.514 --> 00:06:03.047 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the mild warm land of the Klarälven, where the last floating log was
released in 1991 and the old timber float came to an end.

35
00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.496 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Västmanland into view.

36
00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:30.181 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Västmanland is inland on the western shore of Lake Mälaren, west of Stockholm,
with Västerås on the lake and Uppsala just to the north-east.

37
00:06:30.862 --> 00:06:41.056 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The silver mine at Sala funded the Swedish crown for two centuries and goes
155 metres down, with guided tours and a hotel room at the bottom.

38
00:06:41.708 --> 00:06:51.646 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the western men’s land, the silver mine with a hotel at the bottom of
the shaft, and Västerås, a lake port a hundred kilometres from the sea.

39
00:06:52.407 --> 00:06:54.752 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Stockholm into view.

40
00:07:09.622 --> 00:07:21.731 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Stockholm is the small coastal county around the capital, built where Lake
Mälaren meets the Baltic, and it touches only two other counties, Uppsala to
the north and Södermanland to the south.

41
00:07:22.395 --> 00:07:34.295 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The warship Vasa sank on her maiden voyage in 1628 and was lifted out of the
harbour in 1961, and 98 per cent of her timber is original.

42
00:07:34.956 --> 00:07:45.788 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the log islet, the capital on fourteen islands with thirty thousand
more in its archipelago, and the ship that sank on her first voyage.

43
00:07:46.582 --> 00:07:49.090 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Örebro into view.

44
00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:20.824 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Örebro sits in the centre of the country, landlocked, with its largest city of
the same name where the Svartån river runs, and Värmland, Dalarna and
Västmanland around it to the north.

45
00:08:21.484 --> 00:08:30.818 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
In 1810 the Riksdag meeting here chose Bernadotte as crown prince, and that
choice founded the royal house that still reigns in Sweden.

46
00:08:31.474 --> 00:08:42.562 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the gravel bridge in the middle of the country, the castle on its
island in the town, and the place where most of Sweden’s shoes were made until
the 1960s.

47
00:08:43.249 --> 00:08:45.803 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Södermanland into view.

48
00:08:51.809 --> 00:09:01.062 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Södermanland wraps around the southern end of Lake Mälaren and reaches the
Baltic coast south of Stockholm, with Nyköping on the coast and Uppsala to the
north-east.

49
00:09:01.715 --> 00:09:13.313 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Nyköping castle here saw the banquet of 1317, when King Birger shut his
brothers in the dungeon and starved them to death.

50
00:09:13.979 --> 00:09:24.939 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the southern men’s land, often called Sörmland, with the castle where
a king killed his brothers and the densest runestones in the country after
Uppland.

51
00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.358 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Östergötland into view.

52
00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:45.924 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Östergötland is the coastal county on Sweden’s east side below Södermanland,
with the Baltic to the east and Linköping, its largest city, a little way
inland.

53
00:09:46.573 --> 00:09:59.321 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Göta canal crosses the county, 190 kilometres dug by hand between 1810 and
1832, with 58 locks on its way from lake to lake.

54
00:09:59.971 --> 00:10:09.398 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the east land of the Geats, crossed by the hand-dug canal, and
Vadstena, where St Bridget founded the order that spread across Europe.

55
00:10:10.078 --> 00:10:14.258 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Västra Götaland into view.

56
00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:30.704 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Västra Götaland fills the south-west of Sweden on the Kattegat coast, with
Gothenburg in the west, Lake Vänern in the east and Jönköping and Örebro along
its inland edge.

57
00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:42.370 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Gothenburg in it was laid out by Dutch engineers in 1621, which is why it has
canals, and Volvo was founded there in 1927.

58
00:10:43.025 --> 00:10:51.895 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the western land of the Geats, the canal city on the Kattegat and
Lake Vänern, the biggest lake in the European Union.

59
00:10:52.594 --> 00:10:55.021 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Jönköping into view.

60
00:11:00.656 --> 00:11:14.437 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Jönköping lies inland in the south-west of Sweden, on the southern tip of Lake
Vättern, with its largest city of the same name on the shore, Kalmar to the
east and Kronoberg to the south.

61
00:11:15.095 --> 00:11:24.778 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Lake Vättern, Sweden’s second lake, is so clean that the water drawn from it
needs almost no treatment before it can be drunk.

62
00:11:25.438 --> 00:11:33.287 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the town of the safety match at the tip of the clean lake, with the
great inland Vänern lying away to the west.

63
00:11:33.973 --> 00:11:36.481 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Gotland into view.

64
00:11:41.281 --> 00:11:49.547 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Gotland is an island county in the Baltic, lying east of Öland and south of
Stockholm, with Visby on its shore and no land border at all.

65
00:11:50.201 --> 00:11:59.152 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Visby’s ring wall, 3.4 kilometres of it from the 1200s, is the best-preserved
medieval town wall in northern Europe.

66
00:11:59.803 --> 00:12:08.627 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the land of the Gutes, the limestone island where orchids and
truffles grow on bare rock and sea stacks stand in the Baltic.

67
00:12:09.303 --> 00:12:11.985 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Kalmar into view.

68
00:12:16.912 --> 00:12:31.076 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Kalmar runs along the Baltic coast in the south-east of Sweden, with Kalmar
itself at the strait facing the island of Öland, which belongs to this county
too, and Blekinge and Kronoberg to the south.

69
00:12:31.736 --> 00:12:43.973 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Kalmar Union of 1397 put Denmark, Norway and Sweden under one crown for
more than a century, and it was agreed at the castle here.

70
00:12:44.623 --> 00:12:54.642 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the harbour by the stony ground, the union of three kingdoms signed
in Kalmar castle, and the great limestone plain of Öland across the water.

71
00:12:55.334 --> 00:12:57.633 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Halland into view.

72
00:13:02.789 --> 00:13:12.983 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Halland is the narrow coastal county in the south-west, facing the Kattegat
between Västra Götaland and Skåne, with Halmstad as its largest city.

73
00:13:13.634 --> 00:13:24.338 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It was Danish until 1658, and the painters who worked in Halmstad in the 1920s
made this corner of the country its surrealist outpost.

74
00:13:24.994 --> 00:13:33.005 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Sweden’s summer coast with its long sand beaches, and the painters’
colony that made Halmstad the strangest corner of the country.

75
00:13:33.682 --> 00:13:36.109 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Kronoberg into view.

76
00:13:41.037 --> 00:13:50.162 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Kronoberg lies inland in the south of Sweden, with Växjö in its middle,
between Halland on the west and Kalmar on the east, and no sea.

77
00:13:50.812 --> 00:13:59.554 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
IKEA was founded here in Älmhult in 1943 by a seventeen-year-old, and the
first store is now the company’s own museum.

78
00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:09.647 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the crown’s hill, the most forested county in the country, where a
seventeen-year-old started a flat-pack furniture empire in a small shop.

79
00:14:10.333 --> 00:14:14.513 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Blekinge into view.

80
00:14:17.563 --> 00:14:27.966 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Blekinge is the smallest county on Sweden’s mainland, on the Baltic in the far
south-east between Skåne and Kalmar, with Karlskrona in its southern half.

81
00:14:28.627 --> 00:14:38.565 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Karlskrona was founded in 1680 as a naval base for the king, and the harbour
is now a UNESCO world heritage site.

82
00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:48.392 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Sweden’s garden, the mild coast whose oaks were reserved for the
warships of the navy, and the baroque harbour town built for the fleet.

83
00:14:49.078 --> 00:14:51.075 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Skåne into view.

84
00:14:56.241 --> 00:15:07.793 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Skåne is the southern tip of Sweden, across the Øresund from Denmark, with
Malmö on its west coast, Halland to the north-west and Blekinge to the east.

85
00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:16.763 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It is the flattest and most fertile part of the country, about two per cent of
Sweden’s area, and it grows a large share of its food.

86
00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:27.610 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the flat green tip of the country, Danish until 1658 and still
keeping a Danish-sounding r that other Swedes tease.

87
00:15:33.587 --> 00:16:00.299 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
21 regions of Sweden, one for each target of the map: Norrbotten,
Västerbotten, Jämtland, Västernorrland, Gävleborg, Dalarna, Uppsala, Värmland,
Västmanland, Stockholm, Örebro, Södermanland, Östergötland, Västra Götaland,
Jönköping, Gotland, Kalmar, Halland, Kronoberg, Blekinge and Skåne.

88
00:16:00.962 --> 00:16:11.156 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the shape of Sweden from the inside: the regions nest around each
other, and every name on the map belongs somewhere in this one country.
